{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790255974,"nonce":"OiSd9+njjbcV7CM6rQX3HuvqP4k=","message":"The macOS trace failures were return-address signing: cranelift-native enables sign_return_address with the B key on macOS, so every Cranelift prologue is pacibsp and the saved LR carries a signature above bit 46. The M1 runners (macos-14) apply it; macOS 26 machines run plain arm64 processes with the keys off, which is why it only ever failed on CI. 42d24dc strips the bits above the user address space when the saved word names no compiled body, with a_frame_names_its_body_through_a_signed_return_address as the regression. With 041bf94 (Windows frame records) this closes the platform gaps in the walk.","files":null}]}